WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:04.591
This is Ninja, on the Vlaamsekaai in Antwerp.

2
00:00:05.091 --> 00:00:08.705
Its own app, a management panel in 3D and a new website,

3
00:00:08.715 --> 00:00:12.002
for guests who want to know everything and share everything.

4
00:00:12.902 --> 00:00:15.333
The home screen shows what is happening right now:

5
00:00:15.343 --> 00:00:19.249
the temperature in the next slice, the crust, the oak fire,

6
00:00:19.259 --> 00:00:20.848
and how long you will wait.

7
00:00:21.948 --> 00:00:23.331
The spit, live.

8
00:00:23.341 --> 00:00:27.335
Sensors measure the core, the crust, the fire and the weight.

9
00:00:27.435 --> 00:00:30.299
One tap, and you look through a thermal camera.

10
00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:34.962
Ninja takes no reservations.

11
00:00:34.972 --> 00:00:37.480
Join the line digitally from your phone;

12
00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:40.039
regulars move up to the front.

13
00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:42.837
A message, and your table is ready.

14
00:00:44.137 --> 00:00:48.009
The menu is Ninja’s own, with the real prices.

15
00:00:48.059 --> 00:00:50.067
For every dish from the spit you see

16
00:00:50.077 --> 00:00:52.287
what the meat would measure if you ordered now,

17
00:00:52.297 --> 00:00:54.465
and where everything comes from.

18
00:00:56.865 --> 00:01:00.020
Every plate from the spit gets a numbered passport:

19
00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.845
the second it was cut, the degrees in the meat and at the table,

20
00:01:03.855 --> 00:01:06.967
who carved it, and where the lettuce comes from.

21
00:01:07.017 --> 00:01:09.892
Anyone can check it on the website.

22
00:01:11.692 --> 00:01:15.268
The flash camera takes photos in Ninja’s own film look,

23
00:01:15.278 --> 00:01:17.625
with the numbers of your plate on them.

24
00:01:17.675 --> 00:01:18.940
Ready for your story;

25
00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:21.406
the best ones go up on the Wall in the room.

26
00:01:23.906 --> 00:01:25.175
Ninja Match.

27
00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:28.353
Turn it on, and you see who is here tonight.

28
00:01:28.403 --> 00:01:30.844
Send a çay to another table.

29
00:01:30.894 --> 00:01:34.035
If it’s mutual, a conversation begins.

30
00:01:34.085 --> 00:01:36.291
At ten o’clock, everything disappears.

31
00:01:37.691 --> 00:01:40.533
Your own spit, with your name in brass.

32
00:01:40.783 --> 00:01:43.706
The Ninja Clan, from Genin to Kage.

33
00:01:43.956 --> 00:01:46.374
And drops that come only once.

34
00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:50.950
Pay at the table, split the way you like,

35
00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.692
with Payconiq or Apple Pay,

36
00:01:52.702 --> 00:01:55.861
and an invoice via Peppol for business dinners.

37
00:01:58.161 --> 00:02:02.318
The panel shows Ninja live, as a digital twin in 3D:

38
00:02:02.328 --> 00:02:05.008
the guests at their tables, the line outside,

39
00:02:05.018 --> 00:02:07.137
every plate from the pass to the table,

40
00:02:07.147 --> 00:02:09.887
and the drinks guests send each other.

41
00:02:12.587 --> 00:02:17.052
Plus the fire in numbers, with a log for the food safety agency,

42
00:02:17.062 --> 00:02:18.559
the pass with the orders,

43
00:02:18.569 --> 00:02:22.165
and the origin of every batch, with a recall function.

44
00:02:24.265 --> 00:02:25.519
And a new website:

45
00:02:25.529 --> 00:02:29.325
the logo in real 3D leather above the fire, the spit live,

46
00:02:29.335 --> 00:02:33.495
the menu, the origins, and every passport to look up.

47
00:02:35.895 --> 00:02:38.657
Ninja. Every slice, live.

48
00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:41.511
In seven languages, on every phone.
